WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.270
- It's an amazing thing
to be a part of something

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:05.140
so magical, like such a big,
huge thing of pop culture.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.970
Like, did that set in
right away for y'all,

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:09.050
or did it take a few seasons?

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.640
- No, no, it did not set.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.960
I mean, we weren't sure if it
was even gonna work as a show.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.220
'Cause there had not been
any real series on cable

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.220
that were hits at the time.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.720
And when it came out, though,

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.710
it got these crazy reviews
all over the place.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.910
And then it started to get a following,

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.110
and there were billboards
and that kind of thing,

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:30.640
and it just kept going from there.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.873
And now it seems like it's
more popular than it ever was.

00:00:33.873 --> 00:00:36.670
- And that's amazing to be a
part of something that huge.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:39.220
- I think 50 years from now,

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.700
they'll still be watching this thing.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.430
- I know well, it's a
classic, sign of a classic.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:44.664
Well, the show famously ended

00:00:44.664 --> 00:00:46.908
in the middle of a scene and a song.

00:00:46.908 --> 00:00:49.970
No one knows if Tony
Soprano lived or died,

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.793
so what do you think?

00:00:51.793 --> 00:00:53.713
- I think Tony Soprano is alive and well.

00:00:53.713 --> 00:00:56.211
And eating onion rings in New Jersey.

00:00:56.211 --> 00:00:57.044
That's what I think.

00:00:57.044 --> 00:00:57.877
(audience cheering)

00:00:57.877 --> 00:00:59.235
- [Kelly] Okay, that sounds awesome.

00:00:59.235 --> 00:01:00.289
- That's what I think.

00:01:00.289 --> 00:01:02.490
- Okay, I have a feeling

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:03.840
you have a different opinion.
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.821
- Of course he always
got a different opinion.

00:01:05.821 --> 00:01:06.654
- I saw him.

00:01:06.654 --> 00:01:08.157
He did the thinking man pose.

00:01:08.157 --> 00:01:12.440
- I think the cut to black
was his point of view,

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:15.730
and that's the end for the character.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:18.630
That was the last thing he saw
and then it was (indistinct).

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.988
- And Michael is wrong, Kelly.

00:01:19.988 --> 00:01:21.296
(audience laughing)

00:01:21.296 --> 00:01:24.333
Listen to uncle Steve, Michael is wrong.

